{"availability":"available","full":"bloxybighead-svg/Golf-os","name":"Golf-os","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-02T16:01:36Z","updated":"2026-10-11T17:32:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://golf-os-ten.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://golf-os-ten.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:52:46.668Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T20:52:46.668Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T20:52:46.668Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:01.181Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T20:52:46.668Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Golfers consistently underestimate how widely they miss, and then make course-management decisions (which club, where to aim, which tees to play) based on the shot they hoped to hit rather than the pattern they actually produce. Fixing that with data requires thousands of shots per player, which no amateur will ever log.","This project is a shot-dispersion simulator that generates statistically realistic synthetic shot data, validated against a golfer's real launch-monitor data, so dispersion analytics, tee-box recommendations, and aim-point optimization can be built and tested before real users have logged a single shot. It lives inside Golf OS, a Next.js + Supabase golf-tracking app (see the original app below).","Built as a school capstone extension by a 1.9–4 handicap golfer whose own launch-monitor data calibrates and validates the model. Python and Claude Code were used for the coding."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bloxybighead-svg/Golf-os/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d52cbc882eff1a321b5c80ccf0f6fa7460883ecaf53bd8f1734ee531dabd9282","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:01.319Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:01.319Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Golfers consistently underestim